{
  "name": "Get a Slack alert when a Google Maps ranking drops with GeoGridAPI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "fcc3fe92-4efb-59ec-8d44-076f40c40882",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Slack alert when a Google Maps ranking drops\n\nThis workflow measures a business on Google Maps for a keyword every week with a GeoGridAPI geo-grid and posts in Slack only when the ranking gets worse: a higher average rank, fewer points in the top 3, or fewer points in the top 20. Quiet weeks stay quiet.\n\n### How it works\n1. The schedule starts the workflow every Monday at 07:30.\n2. **Run geo-grid** measures the business on a grid around it; the workflow checks it every 20 seconds until it is completed. A failed grid stops with an error and is refunded.\n3. GeoGridAPI returns the change since the previous grid of the same map (same listing, keyword, size and radius).\n4. **Compare with last grid** checks it against your thresholds. The first run only records a baseline.\n5. **Alert Slack** posts the old and new figures and who ranks ahead.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free account on [geogridapi.io](https://geogridapi.io) (500 free credits) and an API key.\n2. Add a **Header Auth** credential named `GeoGridAPI key`: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer gga_live_...`. Select it in the two HTTP Request nodes.\n3. Connect Slack and pick the channel in **Alert Slack**.\n4. Fill in **Settings**: business (\"name, city\"), keyword, grid size, radius, and the thresholds `rankDrop` (places, default 1), `top3Drop` and `foundDrop` (points, defaults 3 and 5).\n\n### Customization tips\n- Cost: 1 credit per point, 49 credits a week for a 7 x 7 grid.\n- Run it daily by changing the schedule; keep the same size and radius so the grids stay comparable.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 800
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4378aa41-f829-5b88-b49d-5d6a874e5c98",
      "name": "Section: schedule and settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. When and what to watch",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 7
